+---
+id: dl-003-validate-task-input-at-the-list-boundary-reject-with-invalid-input
+type: decision-log
+title: "Validate task input at the list boundary, reject with invalid-input"
+status: approved
+---
+
+## Context
+
+Some screens pass whatever the user typed straight to the list, so `TaskList.add`, `.rename` and `.tag`
+can receive a title that is empty or blank, a title over 120 characters, a priority that is none of
+`low`/`normal`/`high` (the `NewTask.priority` and `TaskFilter.priority` static types only constrain
+callers that go through the type checker, not these untyped screens), or a tag that is empty or
+contains a space. `src/domain/` must never throw (`r4-errors-as-result`), so a rejection has to be a
+`Result`, and nothing in the list may change when one happens.
+
+## Decision
+
+- Added `'invalid-input'` to `TodoErrorCode` in `result.ts`, alongside `not-found`, `duplicate` and
+  `invalid-state`.
+- Added three validators to `task.ts`, next to the other task-shape logic they guard: `validateTitle`
+  (trims, rejects empty/blank or over 120 characters trimmed), `validatePriority` (rejects anything not
+  in `PRIORITIES`), `validateTag` (rejects empty, or containing a space). Each returns `Result<string>`
+  or `Result<Priority>`, never throws, and takes a plain `string` input rather than `Priority` for
+  `validatePriority` since the whole point is to check a value that is not statically known to be one.
+- `list.ts`'s `add`, `rename` and `tag` call the matching validator(s) before touching `tasks`: `add`
+  validates title, then priority (if given), then every tag, in that order, before the duplicate-title
+  check; `rename` validates the new title after locating the task but before the duplicate check;
+  `tag` validates before calling `change`. Any validation failure returns that `Result` immediately, so
+  the map is never touched — this falls out of validating before the first write, not from an added
+  rollback path.
+- `untag` was left unvalidated: removing a tag that fails validation is harmless (it simply will not be
+  present, so `removeTag` is a no-op), and the request names only add, rename and tag.
+- `rename`'s existing duplicate-title check still compares against the *validated* (trimmed) target,
+  so behaviour there is unchanged for valid input.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- Callers get a specific, typed reason (`error.code === 'invalid-input'`, with a human-readable
+  `message`) instead of a generic failure or, worse, a corrupted task silently stored.
+- No new dependency was needed (`r1-no-new-dependency`); validation reads no clock and no randomness
+  (`r3-no-clock-or-randomness`); every new exported function carries a TSDoc comment
+  (`r2-tsdoc-on-exports`).
+- `test/list.test.ts` gained characterization-style red-first tests for each rejection path (empty/blank
+  title, over-length title, bad priority, bad tag on add, bad title on rename, bad tag on tag), each
+  also asserting the list is unchanged after the rejection.
