+---
+id: task-003-validate-task-input-title-priority-tags
+type: task
+title: "Validate task input: title, priority, tags"
+status: approved
+---
+
+## Request
+
+Some screens pass whatever the user typed straight to the list, and odd tasks show up. Reject invalid
+input with a clear error that says what is wrong:
+
+- a title that is empty, or only spaces;
+- a title longer than 120 characters;
+- a priority other than `low`, `normal` and `high`;
+- a tag that is empty or contains a space.
+
+Applies when a task is added, renamed or tagged. When input is rejected, nothing in the list changes.
+
+## What I did
+
+- Added `validateTitle`, `validatePriority` and `validateTag` to `src/domain/task.ts`, each returning a
+  `Result` rather than throwing (per `r4-errors-as-result`), with TSDoc comments (per
+  `r2-tsdoc-on-exports`).
+- Added the `'invalid-input'` error code to `TodoErrorCode` in `src/domain/result.ts`.
+- Wired the validators into `TaskList.add`, `.rename` and `.tag` in `src/domain/list.ts`, each checked
+  before any write to the task map, so a rejection changes nothing.
+- Wrote red-first tests in `test/list.test.ts` for every rejection path (empty/blank title, over-120
+  title, invalid priority, invalid tag on add, invalid title on rename, invalid tag on tag), each
+  confirming the failing `code` and that the list is unchanged; confirmed they failed before the
+  implementation and pass after. Full suite: 21/21 passing.
+- Recorded the approach as
+  `dl-003-validate-task-input-at-the-list-boundary-reject-with-invalid-input` (decision-log, submitted,
+  awaiting approval).
+
+## Follow-up
+
+`untag` was deliberately left unvalidated: removing a tag that would fail validation is a harmless
+no-op, and the request only names add, rename and tag.
